WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
- Before we go, I have one more
story to share that I love,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.860
a lesson from one classroom

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.140
all about celebrating good over evil.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.802
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.802 --> 00:00:11.160
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.320
Dan Gill is a middle school teacher

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.760
in Montclair, New Jersey.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.160
He's taught for 52 years and one

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.880
of his most important lessons
doesn't come from a textbook.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.300
It's from this empty chair
he keeps in his classroom.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.170
What does it mean?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.520
Well, let's bring in Mr. Gill

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.580
watching on NBC four
New York to explain it.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.510
Hello? Hi, Mr.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.343
- Gill.

00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:34.710
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.540
Thank you for having me on the show.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.100
- [Kelly Clarkson]
Absolutely. I am honored

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:38.933
to have you on the show, man.

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:41.018
I'm so excited to share
this story with everybody.

00:00:41.018 --> 00:00:43.020
First of all, thank you
for being a teacher.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.243
You are angels walking on this planet.

00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:47.025
(crowd cheering)

00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:48.870
But also, please tell everybody

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.678
about the chair in your room.

00:00:50.678 --> 00:00:53.460
- Yeah, so the, it, it all starts

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.200
with a birthday party that I was invited

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.872
to along with one of my
friends who was named Archie

00:00:58.872 --> 00:01:01.293
and he was an African American.

00:01:02.372 --> 00:01:06.600
And when we arrived at the party the woman

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.430
who's the mother of the student

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.620
looked at us very carefully
when after she opened the door

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.610
and she said that I could go
in, but that Archie couldn't.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.080
And like I was stunned
because I, I said, Why

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:22.913
why can't we go in?

00:01:22.913 --> 00:01:25.260
And she said, Well, we
have no more chairs.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.370
And I said, Well, I've been

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.760
to your house a lot and
I was nine years old

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.850
at the time, and this is in New York City.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.970
And I said, you have plenty

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.220
of chairs and even if you
don't, I'll sit on the floor.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.500
And she said, no, you don't understand.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.040
You can come in.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:42.907
Archie can't

00:01:42.907 --> 00:01:45.450
because there are no more
chairs; at that moment,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.730
like, I understood, you know,
what the code words meant

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.140
and I felt so bad,

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.300
and to see my

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.313
one of my good friends humiliated and

00:01:57.313 --> 00:02:00.090
you know this was an apartment house.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.600
We went down the elevator
seven floors down and big

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.930
big tears were welling up
in our eyes and we went back

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.860
to my house where obviously
we have enough chairs.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.830
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh
man, that is, I love that.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:14.910
Do you, do you explain

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.792
to your students why that chair
is there in your classroom?

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:19.410
Do you tell them that story?
'Cause it's so important.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.430
- Yeah. Absolutely.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.340
And one of the difficult things
is that a teacher has is how

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.200
do you connect, especially
when you teach history

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.450
how do you connect the
students in your class

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.430
to the history that you teach?

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:34.104
And, and I think personal
stories do that for them, and

00:02:34.104 --> 00:02:38.310
what it really represents
for them, and I keep

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.862
on emphasizing it, is the,
the opportunity you have to

00:02:41.862 --> 00:02:46.454
come to a free public school
to get a good education

00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:50.520
and to have empathy for
those people who, who need to

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.315
be advocated for and to, to,
to have a charitable spirit

00:02:55.315 --> 00:03:00.127
towards all who come in
this room with anticipation

00:03:00.127 --> 00:03:03.000
seeking that opportunity.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.930
- Yeah.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.410
- [Dan Gill] And, and that-

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:09.224
- Absolutely. Oh my gosh,
thank you so much just

00:03:09.224 --> 00:03:12.690
for first of all, existing,
what a great heart you have

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.240
and what a great teach
you all to all of us.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.770
We're now in your classroom learning.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.300
That was so cool Mr. Gill, thank you.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.449
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:23.580
And that's not all our season long.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.560
Partner pilot pin makers of g2,

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.060
the go-to pin of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.350
want to celebrate teachers

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.784
like you whose impact on
students is immeasurable.

00:03:30.784 --> 00:03:33.059
So they're gonna give you
a thousand dollars just

00:03:33.059 --> 00:03:34.083
for being you.

00:03:35.346 --> 00:03:37.290
- That's great.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.313
I shouldn't love it.

00:03:39.821 --> 00:03:41.097
- Ah, thank you so much Mr. Gill.

00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:43.260
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.059
Carrie, Washington, Charlize
Theron, Sophia Anne Caruso,

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.233
Salman Janani, Sophia Wiley, Paul Feig,

00:03:51.649 --> 00:03:52.740
and y'all have a great
day and if it's not,

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.640
try and change it.

